"<strong>Q2.</strong> Show that for any circular orbit μ/L = e/(2m_e), whatever the radius and speed. What is μ for the Bohr orbit n, in units of μ_B = eħ/(2m_e)?",
"<strong>Q3.</strong> A 3d electron (l = {#}) is in a field of {#} T. List the allowed values of L_z, the angles L can make with the field, and the energy shift of each state.",
"<strong>Q4.</strong> Silver atoms (one unpaired 5s electron, l = {#}) leave an oven at {#} K. Classical physics predicts what pattern on the screen? Quantum mechanics with only orbital angular momentum predicts what? What is seen, and what does it tell us?",
